## 9. Bounds and side effects

* The oneclick-condition reproduction is a LOCAL STAND-IN for the container's environment (the container
  itself is the authority): the numbers it produced match the container's for both cases, but the
  stand-in cannot prove the container's npm tier.
* `npm install --prefix <tree> cclsp@0.7.0` needs the registry. A checkout that HAS `bun install`ed takes
  the offline copy tier; the oneclick container reaches the registry already (its own case-install does).
* Running the local matrix staged the ast-grep engine into `dist/mpd-package/.toolchain` (the container's
  step 16b2, done here to give `mcp-call`'s call arm its binary) and it was REMOVED again afterwards;
  `install-mcp.ts` also rewrote `~/.mpd/mcp.env`, its documented activation file.
* `skills/**` changed, so `VENDOR_LOCK.json`'s corpus `treeSha` is invalidated: the wave's SINGLE re-pin
  (AGENTS §9/§11) must land in the same commit as this change.
* No git writes were made by this seat (files edited only); the evidence path is
  `evidence/tui/dsh-tui-015/oneclick-reds/2026-10-14T15-50-48Z/`.
